('PUMP-UZ-001', 'Pumping Station No. 2 Modernization — Jizzakh (PPP Investment)', 'Модернизация насосной станции № 2 — Джиззак (ГЧП-инвестиции)', 'Pumping Station No. 2 Modernization — Jizzakh (PPP Investment)', 'Pumping Station No. 2 is located in the Jizzakh region of the Republic of Uzbekistan and is part of the national water resource management system. The station is managed by the Ministry of Water Resources and is scheduled for modernization under the Water Resources Development Concept of the Republic of Uzbekistan for 2020–2030 (Presidential Decree No. UP-6024, dated July 10, 2020). The modernization aims to improve water supply efficiency and advance digital transformation in alignment with the United Nations Global Compact and the UN-Water Initiative.', 'Pumping Station No. 2 is located in the Jizzakh region of the Republic of Uzbekistan and is part of the national water resource management system. The station is managed by the Ministry of Water Resources and is scheduled for modernization under the Water Resources Development Concept of the Republic of Uzbekistan for 2020–2030 (Presidential Decree No. UP-6024, dated July 10, 2020). The modernization aims to improve water supply efficiency and advance digital transformation in alignment with the United Nations Global Compact and the UN-Water Initiative.', 'Uzbekistan', 'Jizzakh Region', 'investment_open', 17, 7760600, 'PPP, pumping_station, Ministry_of_Water_Resources, UNICAP', 40.1033, 69.2233),
('PUMP-UZ-002', 'Korovulbozor Pumping Station Modernization — Bukhara (PPP Investment)', 'Модернизация насосной станции Коровульбозор — Бухара (ГЧП-инвестиции)', 'Korovulbozor Pumping Station Modernization — Bukhara (PPP Investment)', 'The Korovulbozor Pumping Station is located in the Bukhara region of the Republic of Uzbekistan and is part of the national water resource management system. The station is managed by the Ministry of Water Resources and is scheduled for modernization under the Water Resources Development Concept of the Republic of Uzbekistan for 2020–2030 (Presidential Decree No. UP-6024, dated July 10, 2020). The modernization aims to improve water supply efficiency and advance digital transformation in alignment with the United Nations Global Compact and the UN-Water Initiative.', 'The Korovulbozor Pumping Station is located in the Bukhara region of the Republic of Uzbekistan and is part of the national water resource management system. The station is managed by the Ministry of Water Resources and is scheduled for modernization under the Water Resources Development Concept of the Republic of Uzbekistan for 2020–2030 (Presidential Decree No. UP-6024, dated July 10, 2020). The modernization aims to improve water supply efficiency and advance digital transformation in alignment with the United Nations Global Compact and the UN-Water Initiative.', 'Uzbekistan', 'Bukhara Region', 'investment_open', 15, 6189700, 'PPP, pumping_station, Ministry_of_Water_Resources, UNICAP', 39.7747, 64.4286),
