('PUMP-UZ-005', 'Amu-Bukhara-1 Pumping Station Modernization — Bukhara (PPP Investment)', 'Модернизация насосной станции Аму-Бухара-1 — Бухара (ГЧП-инвестиции)', 'Amu-Bukhara-1 Pumping Station Modernization — Bukhara (PPP Investment)', 'The Amu-Bukhara-1 Pumping Station is located in the Bukhara region of the Republic of Uzbekistan and is part of the national water resource management system. The station is managed by the Ministry of Water Resources and is scheduled for modernization under the Water Resources Development Concept of the Republic of Uzbekistan for 2020–2030 (Presidential Decree No. UP-6024, dated July 10, 2020). The modernization aims to improve water supply efficiency and advance digital transformation in alignment with the United Nations Global Compact and the UN-Water Initiative.', 'The Amu-Bukhara-1 Pumping Station is located in the Bukhara region of the Republic of Uzbekistan and is part of the national water resource management system. The station is managed by the Ministry of Water Resources and is scheduled for modernization under the Water Resources Development Concept of the Republic of Uzbekistan for 2020–2030 (Presidential Decree No. UP-6024, dated July 10, 2020). The modernization aims to improve water supply efficiency and advance digital transformation in alignment with the United Nations Global Compact and the UN-Water Initiative.', 'Uzbekistan', 'Amu-Bukhara Region', 'investment_open', 20, 9490100, 'PPP, pumping_station, Ministry_of_Water_Resources, UNICAP', 40.1, 63.8),
('PROJ-INT-DESAL-001', 'NEOM Desalination Megaproject — Red Sea', 'Мегапроект опреснения НЕОМ — Красное море', 'NEOM Desalination Megaproject — Red Sea', 'NEOM — Saudi Arabia''s $500 billion smart city on the Red Sea — requires a fully independent water supply system for 9 million future residents. The project includes a 500,000 m³/day solar-powered reverse osmosis desalination plant, zero liquid discharge technology, and a 100% renewable-energy water supply chain. This is the world''s most ambitious attempt to create a sustainable municipal water system from scratch in a hyper-arid environment.', 'NEOM — Saudi Arabia''s $500 billion smart city on the Red Sea — requires a fully independent water supply system for 9 million future residents. The project includes a 500,000 m³/day solar-powered reverse osmosis desalination plant, zero liquid discharge technology, and a 100% renewable-energy water supply chain. This is the world''s most ambitious attempt to create a sustainable municipal water system from scratch in a hyper-arid environment.', 'Saudi Arabia', 'NEOM, Tabuk Region — Red Sea Coast', 'in_implementation', 14, 1500000000, 'desalination, saudi-arabia, neom, renewable-energy, smart-water, mega-project', 28, 35.5),
('PROJ-INT-SMART-001', 'Singapore Deep Tunnel Sewerage System Phase 2 + NEWater', 'Глубокая тоннельная канализация Сингапура — фаза 2 + NEWater', 'Singapore Deep Tunnel Sewerage System Phase 2 + NEWater', 'Singapore''s DTSS Phase 2 is the world''s most advanced integrated water management system — a $6 billion, 200 km deep tunnel that consolidates all wastewater collection and reclamation. Combined with the NEWater program (advanced wastewater recycling), it makes Singapore the first nation to achieve ''water independence'' despite zero natural water resources, recycling 40% of all water demand.', 'Singapore''s DTSS Phase 2 is the world''s most advanced integrated water management system — a $6 billion, 200 km deep tunnel that consolidates all wastewater collection and reclamation. Combined with the NEWater program (advanced wastewater recycling), it makes Singapore the first nation to achieve ''water independence'' despite zero natural water resources, recycling 40% of all water demand.', 'Singapore', 'Singapore Island — National', 'in_implementation', 9, 6000000000, 'singapore, smart-water, NEWater, wastewater-recycling, water-independence, digital-twin', 1.35, 103.82),
('PROJ-INT-WTE-001', 'Aarhus Water-Energy Nexus — Wastewater to Energy', 'Водно-энергетический проект Орхуса — сточные воды в энергию', 'Aarhus Water-Energy Nexus — Wastewater to Energy', 'Aarhus Vand''s Marselisborg Wastewater Treatment Plant became the world''s first energy-positive wastewater utility in 2015 — producing 150% of its own energy needs by maximizing biogas production from sludge. The plant treats 25 million m³/year for 250,000 people while exporting power to the grid, demonstrating the wastewater-to-energy model that Europe is now mandating for all utilities by 2030.', 'Aarhus Vand''s Marselisborg Wastewater Treatment Plant became the world''s first energy-positive wastewater utility in 2015 — producing 150% of its own energy needs by maximizing biogas production from sludge. The plant treats 25 million m³/year for 250,000 people while exporting power to the grid, demonstrating the wastewater-to-energy model that Europe is now mandating for all utilities by 2030.', 'Denmark', 'Aarhus, Jutland', 'completed', 11, 340000000, 'denmark, wastewater-energy, biogas, energy-positive, circular-economy, EU-directive', 56.15, 10.21),
('PROJ-INT-TRANS-001', 'Central Asia Water-Energy Nexus Agreement — CASWEN', 'Соглашение по водно-энергетическому нексусу Центральной Азии — CASWEN', 'Central Asia Water-Energy Nexus Agreement — CASWEN', 'The Central Asia Water-Energy Nexus Agreement (CASWEN) addresses the fundamental conflict between upstream hydropower states (Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan) and downstream irrigation states (Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan, Turkmenistan). Modeled on the Mekong River Commission and Nile Basin Initiative, CASWEN would establish a legally binding water-sharing framework, a $750M transboundary infrastructure fund, and a regional data-sharing platform — replacing 60 years of ad hoc bilateral agreements.', 'The Central Asia Water-Energy Nexus Agreement (CASWEN) addresses the fundamental conflict between upstream hydropower states (Kyrgyzstan, Tajikistan) and downstream irrigation states (Uzbekistan, Kazakhstan, Turkmenistan). Modeled on the Mekong River Commission and Nile Basin Initiative, CASWEN would establish a legally binding water-sharing framework, a $750M transboundary infrastructure fund, and a regional data-sharing platform — replacing 60 years of ad hoc bilateral agreements.', 'Multi-country', NULL, 'under_development', 7, 750000000, 'transboundary, central-asia, water-diplomacy, governance, water-energy-nexus', 42, 69);
